# shir_nodes/string_contains.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Substring test (lowered from `grep -q`, `case *P*)`).
#
# Backends: Perl index()!=-1, JS .includes(), C strstr(), Rust .contains()
# Fallback: sh2.contains(text, pattern)
#
# The test is the CUT primitives' answer as a boolean: ShIR_TextOps_Cut proves
# `string_contains_sound` — the node is `find_first text pattern != None`, which
# is equivalently "the pattern occurs as a slice of the text", with the empty
# pattern occurring everywhere and the empty TEXT containing only the empty
# pattern. Every backend arm above computes one of those three readings.

# PATTERN: TextOps#glob_contains_sound — the shell form this node lowers is `LIT*`-style
# interior matching (`case *P*)`, `index() != -1`), which in the formal fragment of
# ShIR_TextOps_Glob is `pmatch [PStar, PLit p, PStar]`. Proved: the node's scan and that
# glob match are the same test — `contains_anywhere t p = pmatch [PStar, PLit p, PStar] t`,
# both directions (TextOps#contains_is_a_glob_match / #glob_match_is_contained, via the
# offset-to-split bridge #contains_drop_split).
# BOUNDARY (checked in ShIR_TextOps_Glob: #fragment_is_three_constructors, and the
# one-byte tests #literal_test_cannot_be_a_class / #any_test_is_every_byte /
# #star_test_is_every_string): the fragment has exactly three constructors, so classes,
# ranges, negation, extglob, brace alternation and quoting are outside the model. A
# lowering whose pattern carries one of those is outside this node's contract.
spec: TextOps#string_contains_sound
spec: TextOps#glob_contains_sound

node StringContains
tag "StringContains"
kind expr
# the node body (fields + tag) was lost from this file at HEAD — a doc-only
# copy of cut_at.node's header, so build.rs declared no node and the
# renderer stopped compiling. Restored from the node's own doc contract:
# `text` is the haystack, `pattern` the needle, both any string expression;
# the value is the TEST (JS .includes / Perl index != -1 / rust .contains).
field text: expr
field pattern: expr
